Revision history for Podlite

2.00  2026-11-21
    - follows the Podlite specification 2.0
    - a line scanner with its own input reader replaces Filter::Simple;
      the module needs Perl 5.10.1 and only core modules
    - broken markup stops compilation with an error naming the file and
      line: an unclosed =begin, a stray or mismatched =end, a =begin, =for
      or =end line with no valid block name, or with a name followed by
      neither whitespace nor the end of the line
    - a block name must be followed by whitespace or the end of the line;
      =head1(x) or =Foo::Bar->new stays Perl
    - block names follow the identifier rules of the specification
    - indented directives are recognized for words the specification
      defines; an indented user-defined abbreviated block stays Perl
    - code after =set, =alias, =include and =boundary lines runs; 1.00
      dropped it
    - =data-table rows and =data inside code examples no longer go to
      *DATA; names that only begin with data are not =data
    - the last =data block keeps its trailing bytes; wide characters read
      back through an encoding layer
    - =begin/=end pairs inside verbatim blocks and Markdown fences are not
      markup; markers inside code examples do not end the program
    - a module that uses Podlite no longer replaces the program's
      main::DATA; data reaches the importing package and the packages
      declared in the filtered code
    - a repeated use Podlite keeps data and read position
    - __DATA__ followed by a comment is a marker
    - the notification attribute is spelled :notice in the documentation
    - documentation brought to specification 2.0, links to its
      versioned page

1.00  2025-11-09
    - initial release
    - source filter for Podlite markup language in Perl programs
    - strips Podlite markup during compilation
    - preserves line numbers for accurate error reporting
    - support for embedded data via *DATA filehandle
